--
-- The japa half, book pages 28 to 48: 27 steps from the Namaskara mantras
-- to the sprinkling of the place of japa, ending at the book's own colophon,
-- iti trikaala sandhyaagaayatreejapavidhih. The rite is published here.
--
-- IT ALSO REPAIRS SOMETHING 0048 SHIPPED WITHOUT. All eighteen of part one's
-- steps went in with instruction_ta empty. Every other pooja in this app has
-- Tamil on every step, and proofread said so the moment 0048 was run. The
-- lesson was already recorded in 0033 -- diff a new step's column set against
-- an existing step of the SAME pooja, not against the schema -- and was there
-- to be read. Backfilled here rather than in a file of its own, so the rite is
-- whole in one place. The generator now refuses to emit a step without Tamil,
-- which is the only change that stops it recurring.
--
-- TWO MORE MISPRINTS CORRECTED:
--
--   सायं मन्ध्या गायत्री  ->  सायं सन्ध्या गायत्री
--   Book page 31 sets मन्ध्या in the evening row of the japa sankalpa -- a स
--   as म. The morning row spells सन्ध्या correctly, the roman beside the
--   evening row reads "saayam sandhyaa-gaayatree", and page 37 sets the same
--   word correctly.
--
--   भूरादिससव्याहृतीनाम्  ->  भूरादिसप्तव्याहृतीनाम्
--   Book page 32 has सस where it needs सप्त. The roman beside it reads
--   "bhooraadi saptavyaahrteenaam" and the English gloss on the same page
--   says "The seven vyahrutis beginning with Bhu".
--
-- ABHIVADANAM IS PRINTED AS THE BOOK PRINTS IT, blanks and all. It is not a
-- form the app fills in: the book sets the Apastamba sutra and the Yajus
-- recension in type and leaves dotted rules for the pravaras, the gotra and
-- the name, because whoever is reciting knows their own.
